L0111: Hash syntax is an attribute

The # token begins a supported attribute such as #[derive(Clone)]. Earlier proof spellings using # are not accepted. Write a proof type with @ and construct evidence through prove!, a constructor or a proof-producing function.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/hash_proof_syntax.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```locus
// `#` begins an attribute and nothing else: in a type and in an expression
// it is an error, and the note points at proof types and `_`.
prop Small(n: u8) {
    Is(witness: @(n <= 9)),
}

fn first(n: u8, small: #Small(n)) -> u8 { n }

fn second(n: u8) -> (out: u8, @(out == n)) {
    (n, #{ _ })
}
```

Language, as built: [1.7:1](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.7:1).
